  "melee attachment": {
    "name": "Melee Attachment",
    "packId": "impmal-core",
    "item": {
      "name": "Melee Attachment",
      "type": "modification",
      "img": "modules/impmal-core/assets/icons/modification/modification.webp",
      "system": {
        "notes": {
          "player": "<p>Most commonly known as bayonets, melee attachments affix a long blade to the end of a ranged weapon such as a Lasgun, Autogun or Flamer. Oft times these humble attachments can be the difference between life and death when the enemy bears down upon a warrior.</p><p>A melee attachment functions as a @UUID[Compendium.impmal-core.items.Item.bS4Uy21y8pkp7I7P]{Mundane Sword} when affixed to a Ranged Weapon with the Two-handed Trait. It may be attached or removed as an Action. Wielding a ranged weapon with a melee attachment counts as a melee weapon for the purpose of defending yourself (see @UUID[JournalEntry.hdElQAwiBr5AyoRf.JournalEntryPage.Rjw4KykpjGJlGYEk#melee-attack]{Melee Attacks}). Note that when not attached to a weapon, a typical Melee Attachment counts as a @UUID[Compendium.impmal-core.items.Item.qQ8Y8nmiaTaKgzvs]{knife}.</p>",
          "gm": ""
        },
        "encumbrance": {
          "value": 0
        },
        "cost": 50,
        "availability": "scarce",
        "quantity": 1,
        "category": "combat",
        "usedWith": "Any Ranged Weapon with the Two-Handed Trait.",
